@author Northgrid Electric, System Operations
@date 2026-10-10

kpi Available supply | 5,200 MW | 100% | neutral
kpi Stage 1 | 4,784 MW | 92% of supply | neutral
kpi Stage 2 | 5,044 MW | 97% of supply | bad
kpi Stage 3 | 5,200 MW | 100% of supply | bad

!!! Hospitals, the 911 center and water pumping stations must never be switched off. Confirm they are excluded before any block is opened.

# When to use
Use this runbook when the day-ahead forecast or live demand reaches 92% of available supply (4,784 MW).

! A stage is declared by the Duty Director, never by a single operator.

# Stages
data stages = stage,from,to; Normal,0,4784; Stage 1,4784,5044; Stage 2,5044,5200; Stage 3,5200,5400
chart range stages from=from to=to unit=MW bands=4784,5044,5200 title="Demand thresholds by stage"

cards
### Stage 1: 92% (4,784 MW)
- Issue a conservation alert by text and app to 380,000 customers.
- Ask large industrial customers on interruptible contracts to get ready to reduce load on 30 minutes of notice.
- Confirm that standby generation at 3 peaking plants can start within 20 minutes.
### Stage 2: 97% (5,044 MW)
- Call the demand response program (about 210 MW).
- Start buying emergency imports from the neighboring utility.
- Brief the regulator by phone.
### Stage 3: 100% (5,200 MW)
- Begin rotating outages in blocks A to L.
- Each block is off for at most 60 minutes, in order.
- Never repeat a block before all twelve have been used.

# Steps for rotating outages
1. Get approval
-- 1. The Duty Director approves in the log.
-- 2. The regulator is told within 30 minutes.
2. Protect critical sites
-- 1. Confirm that hospitals, the 911 center and water pumping stations are excluded.
-- 2. Check that the exclusion list was updated this month.
3. Run the blocks
-- 1. Open the first block's feeders.
-- 2. Restore it after 60 minutes at most and open the next.
-- 3. Update the public outage map every 15 minutes.
4. Stand down
-- 1. End rotating outages when demand stays below 95% for 60 minutes.
-- 2. Restore all blocks.
-- 3. File the event report within 24 hours.

!! Blocks run in order A to L, at most 60 minutes each. No block repeats until all twelve have been used.

